@@s129 teacher
@@s130 takeWhile or filter?
@@s131 On <code>LazyList(1, 2, 3, 4)</code> with "is even": <code>takeWhile</code> gives <code>List()</code> (it stops at once on the 1), <code>filter</code> gives <code>List(2, 4)</code> (it skips and continues). In the <code>foldRight</code> version the difference is one word: <code>else empty</code> against <code>else acc</code>.
@@s132 map or flatMap?
@@s133 Look at what <code>f</code> returns. A value (<code>A => B</code>) → <code>map</code>. A list (<code>A => LazyList[B]</code>) → <code>flatMap</code>. With <code>map</code> and an <code>f</code> that gives lists you would get a list of lists.
@@s134 map, filter, headOption: who computes what, and when
@@s135 The <code>…Unfold</code> and <code>…1</code> versions
@@s136 They give <b>the same results</b> as the originals, written in another way: <code>takeWhile1</code> and <code>headOption1</code> with <code>foldRight</code> (ex 6–7), <code>mapUnfold</code>, <code>takeUnfold</code>, <code>takeWhileUnfold</code>, <code>fibsUnfold</code> with <code>unfold</code> (ex 12–13). The code is in the pages <a href="s04-foldright-pigro.html">Lazy foldRight</a> and <a href="s04-infinite-unfold.html">Infinite lists and unfold</a>.
@@s137 Originals, …1 with foldRight, …Unfold
